{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-alerts-watch-app-b-01","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-3","surface":"watch","area":"watch/app","refs":["F-watch-103","F-watch-104","F-watch-113","F-watch-115","FN-L14-watch-app-01","FN-B-run-watch-app-a-01"],"severity":"S3","title":"The watch keeps no record of its own end-of-rest buzzes or workout-start pop-ups","what":"The watch does several things on its own: it buzzes when a rest ends, sets an alarm for that buzz (falling back to a loose alarm that can fire minutes late when exact alarms are not allowed), and opens itself or pops up a 'Workout started' card when a workout starts on the phone. None of this is written to the watch's screen log, the one record support can get through the phone's Help and feedback. That log holds only screen and battery events. So when a member writes 'my watch did not buzz' or 'it buzzed late', nobody can tell whether the buzz fired, when, or that the loose alarm was used.","expected":"Each rest-end buzz, the kind of alarm used for it, and each workout-start open or pop-up (or why it was skipped) adds one short line to the watch's screen log, so a member's report shows what happened.","evidence":["apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/RestAlerts.kt:101-111","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/RestAlerts.kt:126-149","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchState.kt:385-402","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WorkoutStarted.kt:65-116","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/AmbientDiag.kt:27-34","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/AmbientDiag.kt:148-158","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/DiagSend.kt:8-14"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"watch-auto-actions-not-in-diary","who":"members with a watch, and support","how_often":"every rest end and every workout start; matters when a member reports a missed buzz","fix_line":"Write a line to the screen log for each buzz, alarm kind and workout-start pop-up","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-alerts-watch-app-b-02","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-4","surface":"watch","area":"watch/app","refs":["F-watch-103","F-watch-116"],"severity":"S4","title":"The watch's 'Rest is over' card stays up after the set is ticked on the phone when no new rest follows","what":"When a rest ends the watch shows 'Rest is over' both on its own screen and as a card naming the next set. When the member then ticks that set on the phone, the watch's screen moves on, but the card is only taken away when a new rest starts, the workout ends or two minutes pass. If the ticked set starts no rest (rest timer off or set to zero for that exercise), the card keeps telling the member to do a set they already logged.","expected":"When the phone says the set was logged, the watch's 'Rest is over' card goes at the same moment as the screen.","evidence":["apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchState.kt:196-208","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchState.kt:293-297","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/RestAlerts.kt:43-44","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/RestAlerts.kt:88-93","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/RestAlerts.kt:113-123","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/RestAlerts.kt:236-254"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"over-card-kept-after-set-logged","who":"members with a watch who use no rest on some exercises","how_often":"each set ticked on the phone that starts no rest","fix_line":"Remove the 'Rest is over' card whenever the screen's own 'Rest is over' is cleared","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-alerts-watch-app-b-03","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-4","surface":"watch","area":"watch/app","refs":["F-watch-113"],"severity":"S4","title":"A workout started again within 10 minutes does not open the watch or pop up its card","what":"Two signals from the phone can open the watch at a workout's start, so the watch ignores the second for 10 minutes to avoid opening twice. That pause is counted from the last workout start, not tied to the workout. A member who starts a workout, discards it (wrong routine) and starts the right one within 10 minutes gets no watch opening and no 'Workout started' card for the real one, and nothing records why.","expected":"Each new workout opens the watch or pops up its card once, however soon after the last one; only the two signals for the same workout are joined.","evidence":["apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WorkoutStarted.kt:57-61","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WorkoutStarted.kt:65-82","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WorkoutStarted.kt:88-97","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchState.kt:288-292","apps/mobile/android/wear/src/main/java/com/forgeai/wear/WatchState.kt:330-334"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"start-dedupe-window-blocks-new-workout","who":"members with a watch who restart a workout","how_often":"a restart within 10 minutes of the last start","fix_line":"Join the two start signals by the workout's start time, not by a 10 minute window","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
